ech","source_path":"data/traits/structure/homologous_superfamily/cath/nif3-ngg1p-interacting-factor-3-like-3-40-1390-30.yaml","source_record_id":"CATH:3.40.1390.30","source_record_label":"NIF3 (NGG1p interacting factor 3)-like","source_section":"canonical_examples","taxon_id":"NCBITaxon:7227","taxon_label":"Drosophila melanogaster","uniprot_accession":"Q9NK57","unknown_status":"KNOWN_HISTORICAL_DUF"}],"family":{"alphafold_models":12676,"candidate_reasons":["name_matches_duf"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":7,"protein_traits_record":true,"records_by_mech":{"ProteinTraitsMech":6}},"curation_status":"SEEDED","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This family includes the DUF34/metal-binding protein/NIF3 proteins, which are widely distributed across superkingdoms. They were previously annotated as GTP cyclohydrolase 1 type 2 [[cite:PUB00070175]] and, recently, through a comprehensive literature review and integrative bioinformatics analyses it was revealed that annotations for these members were misleading as they were based on a single set of in vitro results examining the NIF3 homolog of Helicobacter pylori [[cite:PUB00070175]]. Actually, they have varied phenotypes with the unifying functional role as metal-binding proteins [[cite:PUB00100327]]. This entry contains several NIF3 (NGG1p interacting factor 3) protein homologues. NIF3 interacts with the yeast transcriptional coactivator NGG1p which is part of the ADA complex, the exact function of this interaction is unknown [[cite:PUB00002954],[cite:PUB00019927]].","domain_architectures":53,"interpro_id":"IPR002678","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":18654,"name":"Duf34/NIF3 (NGG1p interacting factor 3)","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF01784","proteins":18574,"proteomes":16807,"short_name":"DUF34_NIF3","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF01784","structures":16,"taxa":26806,"unknown_status":"KNOWN_HISTORICAL_DUF"},"inputs":